                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "and ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "EmpLive ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontStyle": "italic",
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "systems about Kaimahi working patterns, currently Kaimahi working 96 or more hours in a fortnight and also those working 24 hour cumulative shifts (less than 1 hour between shifts).",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "For more detailed information on the underlying data that the visuals are built upon, please click the question mark button in the top right-hand corner of any page.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "How to use this report:",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "From this page, you can set filters that will be applied throughout the report.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "listType": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "On each page, you can change the filters rather than doing so by navigating back to this page. To access the filters on each page, click the menu icon in the top left-hand corner. Any changes you make will be reflected on all pages.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "listType": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "If you wish to reset the filters and set them back to default, you can click the X button in the top right-hand corner from any page",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "listType": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "At the bottom of each page there is a text box detailing any filters that have explicitly been applied. If nothing is showing for Business Unit, for example, it means that ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "all",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "textDecoration": "underline"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " business units are selected, and there is no active filter applied to that field.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  }
                ],
                "listType": "bullet"
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Dark Orange",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#f47c20"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " indicates a negative result, with",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " light orange",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#f8b079"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": " being negative to a lesser extent. Yellow is used as an alternative colour in the same way for, also for negative results.",
